Kvasir patch: libc src/__support/OSUtil/exit.h
Why:       llvm-libc's internal assertions (LIBC_ASSERT) end in internal::exit, which calls the vendor's
           __llvm_libc_exit. Out of line, the panic record __llvm_libc_exit writes from its return
           address named internal::exit for every assert; inline, it names the assert's own function.
Upstream:  none - a baremetal vendor hook detail; upstream keeps one exit per OS in OSUtil/<os>/.
Proof:     on a device a LIBC_ASSERT (free() of a pointer outside the heap) ends in a panic, cause
           abort, detail 255, whose site symbolises to the asserting function (kvasir_bench.py crash).
Drop when: never while Kvasir provides __llvm_libc_exit and wants the caller's site.

--- a/src/__support/OSUtil/exit.h
+++ b/src/__support/OSUtil/exit.h
@@ -14,7 +14,14 @@
 namespace LIBC_NAMESPACE_DECL {
 namespace internal {
 
-[[noreturn]] void exit(int status);
+// Kvasir: inline, for the baremetal target only Kvasir builds. The vendor's
+// __llvm_libc_exit is then called from the caller's own code (a LIBC_ASSERT)
+// and its return address names that site, not this function.
+extern "C" [[noreturn]] void __llvm_libc_exit(int status);
+
+[[noreturn, gnu::always_inline]] inline void exit(int status) {
+  __llvm_libc_exit(status);
+}
 
 } // namespace internal
 } // namespace LIBC_NAMESPACE_DECL
